# Real, confirmed incident: the first local build of combined_app.py's
# own Dockerfile, before this file existed, copied the repo's real .env
# (live Kalshi/Alpaca/HF/Threads credentials, used for local dev) straight
# into the image via `COPY . .` -- confirmed live when the resulting
# container logged a real Kalshi account balance despite every credential
# env var being explicitly left empty in `docker run`. A container image
# must never carry secrets baked into a layer regardless of where it ends
# up (a registry, a Space, docker history) -- every real secret this app
# needs belongs ONLY in the Space's own runtime secrets/variables, never
# in the image itself. Mirrors .gitignore's own env-file exclusions.
# Wildcard, not just ".env"/".env.*" -- a real incident (see .gitignore's
# identical comment) showed a plain-suffix list misses shapes like
# ".env 2" (a macOS duplicate-file artifact with a space, not a dot).
.env*
!.env.example

.git/
.github/

__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/

venv/
.venv/
env/
ENV/

# Local runtime state (collected data, trained models, job locks/history,
# position state) -- same "regenerated per-deployment, never shipped"
# reasoning as .gitignore's own /data/ exclusion. The Dockerfile creates
# an empty one itself.
/data/
models/*.pkl
models/*.joblib

.kalshi/
.wrangler/

# Local editor/OS cruft
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
.history/

# Dev-only tooling, not needed at runtime
requirements-dev.txt
.claude/
